  "content": {
    "id": "p82-task41-50",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p82-task41-50-shared-instruction",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Solve the following inequalities.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p82-task41-50-part-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2x+1}{x-4}<-3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{11}{5}<x<4$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne4$, $(x-4)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x+1)(x-4)&<-3(x-4)^2\\\\(2x+1)(x-4)+3(x-4)^2&<0\\\\(x-4)(5x-11)&<0\\end{align*}$$\nThe product is negative between its zeroes. Thus $\\dfrac{11}{5}<x<4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task41-50-part-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x+2}{2x-3}>0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-2$ or $x>\\dfrac32$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne\\dfrac32$, $(2x-3)^2>0$. Multiplying by this square gives\n$$ (x+2)(2x-3)>0. $$\nThe product is positive outside its zeroes $-2$ and $\\dfrac32$. Thus $x<-2$ or $x>\\dfrac32$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task41-50-part-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x+1}{x-4}\\ge2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4<x\\le9$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne4$, $(x-4)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+1)(x-4)&\\ge2(x-4)^2\\\\2(x-4)^2-(x+1)(x-4)&\\le0\\\\(x-4)(x-9)&\\le0\\end{align*}$$\nThe polynomial inequality gives $4\\le x\\le9$. Exclude $x=4$, so $4<x\\le9$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task41-50-part-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{x}{x+3}\\le\\dfrac12$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-3<x\\le3$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-3$, $2(x+3)^2>0$. Multiply by this positive quantity.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x(x+3)&\\le(x+3)^2\\\\2x(x+3)-(x+3)^2&\\le0\\\\(x+3)(x-3)&\\le0\\end{align*}$$\nThe polynomial inequality gives $-3\\le x\\le3$. Exclude $x=-3$, so $-3<x\\le3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task41-50-part-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{1-x}\\ge3$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac23\\le x<1$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne1$, $(1-x)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}1-x&\\ge3(1-x)^2\\\\3(1-x)^2-(1-x)&\\le0\\\\(x-1)(3x-2)&\\le0\\end{align*}$$\nThe polynomial inequality gives $\\dfrac23\\le x\\le1$. Exclude $x=1$, so $\\dfrac23\\le x<1$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 62
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task41-50-part-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2-3x}{3-2x}\\le4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<\\dfrac32$ or $x\\ge2$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne\\dfrac32$, $(3-2x)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2-3x)(3-2x)&\\le4(3-2x)^2\\\\(2-3x)(3-2x)-4(3-2x)^2&\\le0\\\\-5(2x-3)(x-2)&\\le0\\\\(2x-3)(x-2)&\\ge0\\end{align*}$$\nThe polynomial inequality gives $x\\le\\dfrac32$ or $x\\ge2$. Exclude $x=\\dfrac32$, so $x<\\dfrac32$ or $x\\ge2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task41-50-part-g",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "g",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{-5x}{3x+4}>2$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac43<x<-\\dfrac8{11}$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-\\dfrac43$, $(3x+4)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}-5x(3x+4)&>2(3x+4)^2\\\\2(3x+4)^2+5x(3x+4)&<0\\\\(3x+4)(11x+8)&<0\\end{align*}$$\nThe product is negative between its zeroes. Thus $-\\dfrac43<x<-\\dfrac8{11}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task41-50-part-h",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "h",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2x}{7-4x}<-5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac74<x<\\dfrac{35}{18}$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne\\dfrac74$, $(7-4x)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x(7-4x)&<-5(7-4x)^2\\\\2x(7-4x)+5(7-4x)^2&<0\\\\(4x-7)(18x-35)&<0\\end{align*}$$\nThe product is negative between its zeroes. Thus $\\dfrac74<x<\\dfrac{35}{18}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task41-50-part-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{5-x}{4-2x}\\ge-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<2$ or $x\\ge3$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne2$, $(4-2x)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}(5-x)(4-2x)&\\ge-(4-2x)^2\\\\(5-x)(4-2x)+(4-2x)^2&\\ge0\\\\6(x-2)(x-3)&\\ge0\\end{align*}$$\nThe polynomial inequality gives $x\\le2$ or $x\\ge3$. Exclude $x=2$, so $x<2$ or $x\\ge3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p82-task41-50-part-j",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "j",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1-4x}{2x+3}>-6$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x<-\\dfrac{19}{8}$ or $x>-\\dfrac32$.",
          "worked": "For $x\\ne-\\dfrac32$, $(2x+3)^2>0$. Multiply by this square.\n$$\\begin{align*}(1-4x)(2x+3)&>-6(2x+3)^2\\\\(1-4x)(2x+3)+6(2x+3)^2&>0\\\\(2x+3)(8x+19)&>0\\end{align*}$$\nThe product is positive outside its zeroes. Thus $x<-\\dfrac{19}{8}$ or $x>-\\dfrac32$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      }
    ]
  },
